From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP land corridor entities on loaded kept-edge pads

0059 skipped unload dests so player relocate would not nested-syncLoad.
Pads were the farthest view-distance rim (chunk 18), so relocate moved 0
and packed-spawn carve aborted. Prefer nearest kept-edge chunks that
are already loaded; still never getChunk(load) / 7-arg teleportTo for
players. Carve stays on.
Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/YapCorridorPlanner.java
+++ b/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/YapCorridorPlanner.java
@@ -285,14 +285,17 @@
                     final int cx = CoordinateUtils.getChunkX(key);
                     final int cz = CoordinateUtils.getChunkZ(key);
                     final int along = plan.cutOnX() ? cx : cz;
-                    // Distance from nearest corridor edge (chunks) — prefer strip tips.
+                    // Distance from nearest corridor edge (chunks).
                     final int dist = leftSide
                             ? (plan.lo() * sectionSize) - along
                             : along - ((plan.hi() + 1) * sectionSize - 1);
                     scored.add(new int[]{cx, cz, dist});
                 }
             }
-            scored.sort((a, b) -> Integer.compare(b[2], a[2]));
+            // Nearest kept-edge first. Farthest "strip tips" sit on the view-distance rim
+            // (e.g. chunk 18) — not loaded, so relocate moved 0 and carve aborted; force-loading
+            // those tips then PlayerSpawnFinder-stalled the region after split.
+            scored.sort((a, b) -> Integer.compare(a[2], b[2]));
             final int n = Math.min(max, scored.size());
             final int[][] out = new int[n][];
             for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {

